WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.430
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.900
PRESENTER: The next
speaker is Hans Beta,

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.400
who's known in the
physics community

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.400
as a person who knows
everything, and has

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.180
done almost everything.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.540
I remember when I first--

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:25.590
no, no, that's wrong--

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.410
I remember at the
early Rochester

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.589
meetings on high energy physics,
whenever there was a question--

00:00:35.057 --> 00:00:36.390
"Has this experiment been done?"

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:37.530
"Has this calculation
been done?"

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:38.738
"What is the result of this?"

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.770
"What is known about this?"--

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:44.160
automatically, every head
turned to Professor Beta.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.414
And his answer was awaited,
and furthermore believed.

00:00:46.414 --> 00:00:47.580
And he always answered, too.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:54.760
There probably is no field of
physics to which he has not

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.940
made an important contribution.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:02.270
He received a
Nobel Prize in 1967

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.570
for the discovery
of the carbon cycle

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:07.910
as a source of energy
generation in the sun.

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.520
Professor Beta was
born in Germany,

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:17.560
came to the United States
as a refugee from the Nazis.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:23.020
He arrived at Cornell in
1935, and more or less has

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.300
been there ever since, with
the exception, of course,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.980
of the years of the
Second World War,

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:36.380
where he worked here for a
while, and then in Los Alamos,

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:42.600
where he was central
in the construction

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.639
of the first nuclear weapons.

00:01:44.639 --> 00:01:46.680
He was the leader of the
theoretical group there.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.440
Ever since, while conducting--
while engaging actively

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.200
in physics research
and teaching,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:06.540
he has worked rationally
and effectively

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:15.540
to exploit and to understand
and to contain the nuclear fire

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.190
which he helped to invent.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:24.930
He was my thesis
advisor 38 years ago.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.546
It was hard.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.861
[LAUGHTER]

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.750
But I learned a
lot and survived.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.700
So it's a real pleasure
to welcome him back

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.290
to MIT, Professor Beta.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:41.126
His title today is
Solar Neutrinos.

00:02:41.126 --> 00:02:44.598
[APPLAUSE]

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.918
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:03:06.918 --> 00:03:09.398
PRESENTER: Yes, okay, let
me show you how that works.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.960
Say something.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.242
BETA: Okay.

00:03:17.242 --> 00:03:19.500
PRESENTER: I think so.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.116
Let me show you how this works,
so you can turn it on and off.

00:03:23.116 --> 00:03:24.490
BETA: I think I'm
following that.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:24.940
PRESENTER: Are you
going to use the--

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:25.585
BETA: Yes.

00:03:25.585 --> 00:03:26.251
PRESENTER: Okay.

00:03:26.251 --> 00:03:28.944
It turns on by pushing
the lever at the bottom.

00:03:36.384 --> 00:03:40.352
BETA: Oh, it's practically in--

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:57.210
[? Friesis, ?] thanks
for the welcome.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:03.150
I want to correct your
introduction by one point.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.073
I have never worked on general
relativity, and I don't--

00:04:07.073 --> 00:04:07.920
[LAUGHTER]

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.912
--don't intend to do so.

00:04:09.912 --> 00:04:12.272
[LAUGHTER]

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:23.290
I'm happy to be here to
join in congratulations to

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:28.920
[? Filmores. ?] But it is
also a sad occasion for me.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:34.370
I'm quite used to getting
old, but it is very depressing

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.406
if young people get old, also.

00:04:37.406 --> 00:04:41.300
[LAUGHTER]

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:49.070
When I met Phil, he was
28, and a very young man.

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:55.010
And now, they tell me he is
70, which is hard to believe.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:58.580
But one thing has
remained unchanged.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:07.490
He always gave us terribly
exciting ideas, insights,

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.090
and he still is at this today.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:17.420
So I wish, Phil, that you
will remain in this situation

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:20.520
for many years to come.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.240
Now, I have to warn you
all that this talk will

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:28.480
be very different
from Dr. Sagen's talk.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:36.200
It is scientific, and it
will contain a number--

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:40.284
even a number of algebraic
formulae that's terrible.

00:05:40.284 --> 00:05:43.620
[LAUGHTER]

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.800
I am going to talk
about the subject that--

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:51.280
[LAUGHTER]

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:59.030
--has been very active for the
last year, namely the subject

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:01.240
of neutrinos from the sun.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:08.320
For many years, this
has been a great puzzle.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:12.010
And to talk about
that, let me start

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:17.260
by telling you the nuclear
reactions which are supposed

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.350
to go on in the sun.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:22.330
They are listed here.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:28.690
And many of them
could use neutrinos.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:32.160
The fundamental the
action, of course, is the--

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:41.020
this doesn't seem to work--

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:47.500
the fundamental
reaction is the top one,

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:53.920
which is the current of two
protons giving a deuteron,

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.210
a positron, and a neutrino.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:04.810
And then, most of the deuterons
which are formed in this way

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:09.130
finally go to this
reaction, making Helium 4.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:12.530
That gives the big energy.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.980
But occasionally,
they make Bavarium 7.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:22.990
which that happens
maybe one time in 1,000.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:27.700
And Bavarium 7, then,
emits another neutrino.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:33.790
And then again, in
a very rare event,

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:37.360
Bavarium 7 will
capture another proton

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:41.530
and give a very odd
nucleus, Boron 8,

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:50.410
which produces neutrinos of
tremendous energy, 14MAB.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:54.630
Here, I have given the energies.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:58.220
C means continuous spectrum.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:05.410
And this is the maximum energy
of the continuous spectrum.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:11.450
In two reactions, you get
a definite energy neutrino.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:19.000
Well, the question is, can
you observe the neutrinos?

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:26.140
It is very difficult to observe
neutrinos of about one MAB.

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:29.320
That is well known.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.860
And it is also
well known that it

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.909
gets a little easier if the
neutrinos have higher energy.

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:44.800
In this connection, then,
Willie Fowler and John Bacon

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:48.460
had a very good idea.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:56.810
They said, well, we
might use Chlorine 37.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:59.920
There is a state
in Argon 37, which

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:04.000
is very similar to
the Chlorine 37 state.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.240
It's a so-called analog state.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:15.160
And therefore, the
transition, the capture,

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:19.940
of a neutrino by Chlorine
37, giving these analog

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:24.640
states in 37, which is
highly excited by six

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:27.580
million electron watts--

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.300
this is a super-allowed
transition,

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:36.070
that is, the transition
is as easy as any neutrino

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.370
capture can ever be.

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:44.790
And so they decided,
let's take Chlorine 37

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:49.740
and observe the Argon
37 which is formed.

00:09:52.250 --> 00:10:01.240
Ray Davis of Brookhaven, now of
the University of Pennsylvania,

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:07.100
has now tried to observe the
capture of solar neutrinos

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.520
for nearly 20 years.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:13.320
He uses a [? tanker ?]
of carbon tetrachloride.

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:18.190
He flushes the argon
out by helium and argon,

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:21.190
puts the argon into
a Geiger counter,

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:27.700
and uses the decay of
Argon 37 which takes place

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:32.560
by capture of an atomic
electron in the [? cache, ?]

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:35.290
giving Chlorine
37 and a neutrino.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:38.870
Of course, you can't observe
that neutrino, either.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:42.210
But you can observe
that the resulting

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:45.576
atom is missing a K electron.

00:10:45.576 --> 00:10:50.620
Thereupon, it emits
X-rays of a few kilobytes.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.970
And those you can observe.

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:06.610
This is the principle
of the observation.

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:13.490
But-- and indeed, Davis
did observe neutrinos,

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:19.810
but only about a third
of the predicted number.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:30.450
This is summarized in
an article by Davis

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:36.960
and two collaborators
going back to 1981.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.015
Well, so what's wrong?

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:44.950
The main person who
investigated this problem

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:49.900
has been John Bacon of the
Institute of Advanced Studies.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:57.670
And He has tried almost
anything in the theory

00:11:57.670 --> 00:12:03.850
of either nuclear reactions
or the constitution of the sun

00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:08.220
to try and clear up this
puzzle, to no avail.

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:20.300
It just doesn't remove
the discrepancy.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:26.390
The way they go about it is
that maybe the temperature

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:31.640
in the center of the
sun is lower than

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:35.320
has been generally supposed.

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:39.560
And for that purpose,
they need information

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:43.125
about the opacity
of solar material

00:12:43.125 --> 00:12:47.240
and the different conditions,
density, and temperature.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:51.110
There is a lot of
contributions by people

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:54.830
at Los Alamos and Livermore.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:58.010
But the result
remained the same.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:04.280
There is a discrepancy by
a factor of 3, or maybe 4.

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:07.290
At the same time, Willie
Fowler and his group,

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:13.980
experimenters group, at Cal Tech
have re-examined the nuclear

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:26.710
reactions, and have found that
the cross-section measurements

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:31.150
for the reaction leading to
Bavarium 7 or to Boron 8,

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:34.280
that these measurements
were correct,

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:38.870
in spite of some people
from other laboratories--

00:13:38.870 --> 00:13:42.970
go ahead-- doubted that.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:53.130
Well, the whole problem was
re-examined very carefully

00:13:53.130 --> 00:14:03.310
in 1982 by Bahcall and others
in a very beautiful paper

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:07.580
in the views of modern
physics, in which they discuss,

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.770
in particular,
[? probable ?] errors

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:13.190
of each step of the argument.

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:17.480
Of course, one point in
the argument everybody

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:20.870
believes, namely that the
proton-proton reaction

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:24.110
makes the energy in the sun.

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:30.410
Not only is it the
logical thing to assume,

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:35.600
but in addition, the general
idea of thermonuclear reactions

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:43.640
in stars has led to a very
detailed understanding

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:46.760
of the further
evolution of stars,

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:49.970
and in particular,
all the details

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:56.220
of the red giant
formation and evolution.

00:14:56.220 --> 00:15:02.840
I especially asked
Bahcall the other day

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:06.200
in a long telephone
conversation,

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:09.440
how sure is he of his results?

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:14.630
And he said, well, we have
gone through all the steps.

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:23.760
We have even results with
three times the standard error.

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:30.050
I don't believe there is any
way to escape the conclusion.

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:35.300
Well, one way was once
proposed by Willie Fowler.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:38.630
He called it the
Desperate Theory.

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:45.800
Everybody knows that the
light comes out of the sun

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:49.710
only after some 5
or 10 million years.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:56.030
So what we see today is
energy which was produced

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:59.490
maybe 10 million years ago.

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:05.480
So maybe the sun was hotter
in those days, more luminous

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:11.150
than it is today, which would
be a rather sad conclusion

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:15.950
because it would predict that
we would go into a severe ice

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:21.650
age in a few million years.

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:25.670
That's less threatening
than nuclear winter,

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:33.440
but still not very promising.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:37.570
Bahcall and others
made a modified theory

00:16:37.570 --> 00:16:41.150
whose results are given here.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:43.610
But in the meantime,
they have gone back

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:49.270
to the theory of 1982.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:54.440
The theory after all
corrections predicts

00:16:54.440 --> 00:17:02.850
that you should observe
on Earth about 6 SNU.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:03.740
That's a funny unit.

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:08.089
Admit It only-- and
I won't explain it.

00:17:08.089 --> 00:17:17.078
It tells you how many counts
Mr. Davis ought to observe.

00:17:17.078 --> 00:17:20.930
But this experiment
gives only 2 SNU.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:29.480
Now, it is somewhat
frustrating to rely

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:33.695
on that funny nucleus, Boron 8.

00:17:33.695 --> 00:17:37.250
It would be much nicer
to observe directly

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:42.500
the neutrinos which come from
the combination of two photons

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:48.260
because we know exactly
how often that must happen,

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:51.170
because that gives
us the energy which

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:59.560
the sun emits every second,
the so-called solar constant.

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:08.440
Well, to avoid the [? lions ?]
on the rare side chain,

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:13.830
it was proposed many years ago
to use a different detector,

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:16.940
namely Gallium 71.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:21.140
And the only thing that's
wrong with that proposal

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:25.310
is that gallium is a very
rare element, and therefore

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:26.570
terribly expensive.

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:32.780
But it obviously was
an important experiment

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:40.830
to do, to find out the
solution to this puzzle.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:49.370
Well, the National Science
Foundation unfortunately

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:52.610
rejected the proposal
several times

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:56.120
to carry out this experiment.

00:18:56.120 --> 00:19:00.860
The Europeans are somewhat
more open to suggestions,

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:03.410
so this experiment
is going to be

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:09.740
done by a collaboration of
Italian, French, and German

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:14.090
physicists, which
will be carried out

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:20.840
in Gran Sasso in Italy,
and is being started now.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:25.820
This gallium experiment
measures directly

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:35.180
the neutrinos which are made
in the proton-proton reaction.

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:39.800
And I have written down
here the capture rates

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:47.360
in these funny units,
SNU, for three detectors.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:50.870
Don't pay any attention
to the lithium.

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:56.540
The chlorine which has been used
observes practically nothing

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:59.120
from the proton-proton reaction.

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:07.700
And the observation comes mostly
from Bavarium 7 and Boron 8.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:11.690
By contrast, gallium
would observe mostly

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:16.070
proton-proton neutrinos,
some, Bavarium 7,

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:18.650
and very few, Boron 8.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:22.550
It also would give
a lot more SNU.

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:28.010
In gallium, the neutrino
capture leads to germanium.

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:36.050
And germanium being an analog
of carbon in the Periodic Table,

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:40.880
lends itself to a very
ingenious detection

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:43.610
scheme proposed by Davis.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.950
He's a good chemist.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:51.020
You make germanium.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:59.380
So the problem remains, why
are there only one third

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:01.850
as many neutrinos as
there ought to be?

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:12.850
It was suggested fairly
early that maybe neutrinos

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:15.840
transform into each other.

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:21.730
Namely, we know there are
different kinds of neutrinos,

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:26.320
electron neutrinos, and muon
neutrinos, and tau neutrinos.

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:35.770
And it was suggested that
maybe these neutrinos are not

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:40.450
the ones which
propagate in free space.

00:21:40.450 --> 00:21:47.630
And that's a very standard
occurrence in particle physics.

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:52.090
You know about it probably
in the case of K mesons.

00:21:52.090 --> 00:21:54.490
And there are many
other examples.

00:21:54.490 --> 00:22:01.250
The particles which interact
with other particles

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:06.070
are usually not the
same as the particles

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:09.240
which propagate in free space.

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:17.490
So then, you assume that
free neutrinos are not

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:19.770
equal to these.

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:24.870
And if that is
so, then neutrinos

00:22:24.870 --> 00:22:29.300
which I should call Neu-1
and Neu-2 will propagate.

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:34.120
And that will have the
consequence that in free space,

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:39.220
neutrinos oscillate between
electron neutrinos and mu

00:22:39.220 --> 00:22:42.360
neutrinos.

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:44.790
[? Linus ?] claimed
at one time that he

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:48.360
had observed such
oscillations using

00:22:48.360 --> 00:22:51.780
the neutrinos from the
Savannah River Reactor.

00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:56.610
But later experiments did
not confirm his results.

00:22:56.610 --> 00:23:01.600
In fact, experiments
recently done at CERN

00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:11.100
find a certain result which
involves two quantities,

00:23:11.100 --> 00:23:16.320
namely the difference in
mass of these neutrinos

00:23:16.320 --> 00:23:19.590
and the angle of coupling.

00:23:22.525 --> 00:23:25.470
I go into that a
little more later.

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:33.090
Namely, the electron neutrino
is not quite the neutrino Neu-1,

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:37.380
but they are off by a
certain angle, theta.

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:42.120
And the CERN experiments
show that the square

00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:47.160
of the mass difference times
square of twice that angle

00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:52.380
must be less than 0.03
electron watts square.

00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:56.470
This is the dimension
because of the mass.

00:23:56.470 --> 00:24:01.350
The direct experiments on the
mass of the electron neutrino

00:24:01.350 --> 00:24:06.180
show probably by now that this
mass is less than 10 electron

00:24:06.180 --> 00:24:10.420
watts, very far
from this number.

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:14.230
Now, if oscillations
were to exist,

00:24:14.230 --> 00:24:17.070
then the electron
neutrinos from the sun

00:24:17.070 --> 00:24:21.300
might be converted into
either mu or tau neutrinos

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:23.520
on their way to the Earth.

00:24:23.520 --> 00:24:27.270
For this, you need a mass
difference greater than 10

00:24:27.270 --> 00:24:30.040
to minus 13.

00:24:30.040 --> 00:24:34.710
But you would need desperately
that the coupling angle would

00:24:34.710 --> 00:24:41.880
be very large, namely that the
free neutrinos are maximally

00:24:41.880 --> 00:24:46.470
different from the
neutrinos interacting

00:24:46.470 --> 00:24:49.740
with electrons or mus.

00:24:49.740 --> 00:24:52.660
That is very unlikely.

00:24:52.660 --> 00:25:01.740
But it can-- a priori, it
cannot be ruled out completely.

00:25:04.660 --> 00:25:11.000
So this was the
situation until recently.

00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:16.710
And recently, two Russian
scientists [? Michraiv ?]

00:25:16.710 --> 00:25:22.620
and [? Smirnov ?] proposed
a theory which I believe is

00:25:22.620 --> 00:25:23.610
the correct theory.

00:25:26.550 --> 00:25:31.800
And they use the
mixing of neutrinos,

00:25:31.800 --> 00:25:39.670
but in a much more
intelligent original way.

00:25:39.670 --> 00:25:47.520
Then I'll discuss
in the last slide.

00:25:47.520 --> 00:25:50.630
I assume only two
neutrino types, electron

00:25:50.630 --> 00:25:53.240
and mu neutrinos.

00:25:53.240 --> 00:25:58.740
And in vacuum, they are coupled.

00:25:58.740 --> 00:26:05.430
In terms of the free
neutrinos, Neu-1 and Neu-2,

00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:11.690
N-1 commonly [? writes ?] that
the electron neutrino is cross

00:26:11.690 --> 00:26:16.020
of a certain coupling [? and ?]
with theta times the free

00:26:16.020 --> 00:26:20.400
neutrino Neu-1 plus
sine theta, times Neu-2.

00:26:20.400 --> 00:26:26.020
And the mu neutrino, of
course, is orthogonal to that.

00:26:26.020 --> 00:26:34.720
Then if the free neutrinos
have masses, M2 and M1,

00:26:34.720 --> 00:26:41.670
you can write the mass
matrix in this form.

00:26:41.670 --> 00:26:43.470
There is a diagonal
term which is

00:26:43.470 --> 00:26:46.530
of no relevance, plus
another term which

00:26:46.530 --> 00:26:50.010
contains the difference
of the two masses,

00:26:50.010 --> 00:26:57.150
and times this very simple
matrix, which is non diagonal.

00:26:57.150 --> 00:27:00.510
In terms, the
[? first term ?] refers

00:27:00.510 --> 00:27:07.180
to electron neutrinos, the
second one to mu neutrinos.

00:27:07.180 --> 00:27:14.870
Now so far, it is no
different from the last slide.

00:27:14.870 --> 00:27:19.570
But now, they make
use of a theory which

00:27:19.570 --> 00:27:29.650
was developed by
Wolfenstein of Carnegie Tech

00:27:29.650 --> 00:27:35.670
and published in
Physics Review in 1978.

00:27:35.670 --> 00:27:39.730
And he says as follows.

00:27:39.730 --> 00:27:45.040
Neutrinos-- when
neutrinos are in matter,

00:27:45.040 --> 00:27:49.180
then all neutrinos
interact with matter

00:27:49.180 --> 00:27:53.230
by means of the
neutral weak current.

00:27:53.230 --> 00:27:55.300
But that's of no
interest because it's

00:27:55.300 --> 00:27:57.610
the same for all neutrinos.

00:27:57.610 --> 00:28:01.310
It doesn't help convert
one into the other.

00:28:01.310 --> 00:28:07.940
However, the electrons also
will interact with the electron

00:28:07.940 --> 00:28:15.980
neutrinos, and none other,
by the charge weak current

00:28:15.980 --> 00:28:21.540
in which an electron
is absorbed by a proton

00:28:21.540 --> 00:28:26.500
and becomes a neutrino
plus a neutron.

00:28:26.500 --> 00:28:33.180
And this has the consequence
that there is effectively,

00:28:33.180 --> 00:28:38.470
in matter, a potential
energy for neutrinos which

00:28:38.470 --> 00:28:41.020
is the universal
Faraday constant,

00:28:41.020 --> 00:28:46.995
g multiplied by the electron
density, a number of electrons,

00:28:46.995 --> 00:28:48.470
for aggregate volume.

00:28:51.730 --> 00:28:57.970
So far, the
Wolfenstein theory, it

00:28:57.970 --> 00:29:05.770
says then that the relation
between momentum and energy

00:29:05.770 --> 00:29:08.950
of a neutrino goes like this.

00:29:11.890 --> 00:29:15.220
The momentum square
plus mass square

00:29:15.220 --> 00:29:19.220
is not equal to E square,
the energy square,

00:29:19.220 --> 00:29:25.930
but energy minus the
potential energy squared.

00:29:25.930 --> 00:29:29.950
And this potential energy,
which only exists for electron

00:29:29.950 --> 00:29:32.110
neutrinos--

00:29:32.110 --> 00:29:38.880
I expand this-- is equivalent
to having an extra mass

00:29:38.880 --> 00:29:43.030
for electron neutrinos,
which is equal to 2E,

00:29:43.030 --> 00:29:49.840
twice the neutrino energy,
times that potential energy.

00:29:49.840 --> 00:29:57.990
And so now, my mass matrix gets
added to it, an interaction

00:29:57.990 --> 00:30:02.620
term, which is this 2EV.

00:30:02.620 --> 00:30:07.300
And that can be
written in this way.

00:30:07.300 --> 00:30:11.050
It's proportional to the
density of the matter,

00:30:11.050 --> 00:30:14.740
and to the energy
of the neutrino.

00:30:14.740 --> 00:30:17.140
And I call that A.

00:30:17.140 --> 00:30:22.030
Now, I add this to
the mass matrix.

00:30:22.030 --> 00:30:27.790
And this will add to
just to the electron

00:30:27.790 --> 00:30:31.510
part of the mass matrix,
electron neutrino part.

00:30:31.510 --> 00:30:34.780
It will add a term here.

00:30:34.780 --> 00:30:38.360
And I wrote it in
such a way that I

00:30:38.360 --> 00:30:45.460
added one half A here and minus
one half A for the mu neutrino.

00:30:45.460 --> 00:30:49.000
And delta here is the
difference in mass,

00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:57.160
the mass of the, essentially,
mu neutrino minus the mass

00:30:57.160 --> 00:30:59.730
of the electron neutrino.

00:30:59.730 --> 00:31:06.160
And remember, you always have
to use the square of the masses.

00:31:06.160 --> 00:31:11.470
Now, therefore,
obviously, when you

00:31:11.470 --> 00:31:15.430
would look at this
equation, you see

00:31:15.430 --> 00:31:20.350
that the difference in
masses becomes smallest

00:31:20.350 --> 00:31:29.170
when the A, which is
proportional to the density,

00:31:29.170 --> 00:31:33.970
is equal to delta
times cosine 2 theta.

00:31:33.970 --> 00:31:39.700
And then, you have a minimum
in the difference of the two

00:31:39.700 --> 00:31:41.470
masses.

00:31:41.470 --> 00:31:47.130
And I will show you a
curve of what that--

00:31:47.130 --> 00:31:48.730
of the consequence of that.

00:31:51.610 --> 00:31:58.720
Namely, there are
two possible values

00:31:58.720 --> 00:32:02.440
for the mass square
of a neutrino.

00:32:02.440 --> 00:32:07.200
If you have no
density of electrons,

00:32:07.200 --> 00:32:09.580
then you have the
electron neutrino here

00:32:09.580 --> 00:32:14.830
at the low mass, no
neutrino at a higher mass.

00:32:14.830 --> 00:32:21.610
But when you get to the
point where this condition is

00:32:21.610 --> 00:32:28.680
satisfied, that A is equal to
the difference of mass square,

00:32:28.680 --> 00:32:34.030
that's this point,
then at this point--

00:32:34.030 --> 00:32:38.170
you can probably not
see that faint line--

00:32:38.170 --> 00:32:40.870
at this point, the
electron neutrino

00:32:40.870 --> 00:32:43.900
would get a bigger mass
than the mu neutrino.

00:32:43.900 --> 00:32:48.430
But there is the
non-diagonal term

00:32:48.430 --> 00:32:53.560
in the matrix, which means that,
actually, the curves do not

00:32:53.560 --> 00:32:54.850
cross.

00:32:54.850 --> 00:33:00.790
But this curve which starts
as the electron neutrino

00:33:00.790 --> 00:33:06.460
ends up at high electron
density as the mu neutrino,

00:33:06.460 --> 00:33:09.250
and vise versa.

00:33:09.250 --> 00:33:14.090
And so, this means, then,
a very interesting thing.

00:33:14.090 --> 00:33:17.750
And that's now the
theory of [? Michraiv ?]

00:33:17.750 --> 00:33:24.590
and [? Smirnov. ?]
If you start--

00:33:30.180 --> 00:33:37.920
well, let me first say that
for our given neutrino energy,

00:33:37.920 --> 00:33:44.790
there is a certain density at
which the two curves cross.

00:33:44.790 --> 00:33:52.020
And that density is determined
by the difference in mass

00:33:52.020 --> 00:33:56.610
of mu neutrino and
electron neutrino,

00:33:56.610 --> 00:33:59.350
and by the universal
[? Faraday ?] constant,

00:33:59.350 --> 00:34:00.540
which we know very well.

00:34:03.120 --> 00:34:10.280
So at present, the difference of
the masses of the two neutrinos

00:34:10.280 --> 00:34:12.400
is not known.

00:34:12.400 --> 00:34:16.320
But it surely is a
constant of nature.

00:34:16.320 --> 00:34:22.500
And therefore, this lambda
is a certain number,

00:34:22.500 --> 00:34:23.489
which we don't know.

00:34:23.489 --> 00:34:25.610
But it's a number.

00:34:25.610 --> 00:34:29.159
And now, let's
assume that neutrinos

00:34:29.159 --> 00:34:33.940
are produced at a
certain density, one

00:34:33.940 --> 00:34:36.360
near the center of the sun.

00:34:36.360 --> 00:34:39.659
Then as they travel
out through the sun,

00:34:39.659 --> 00:34:44.520
they will go through
this resonance

00:34:44.520 --> 00:34:49.340
if their energy is
greater than the energy--

00:34:49.340 --> 00:34:51.840
than a certain
critical energy which

00:34:51.840 --> 00:34:57.090
is equal to that lambda
divided by the density

00:34:57.090 --> 00:34:59.580
at the center of the sun.

00:34:59.580 --> 00:35:04.750
If, however, the-- so
if this is the case,

00:35:04.750 --> 00:35:14.160
then they were automatically
run down the green curve,

00:35:14.160 --> 00:35:19.560
starting out as electron
neutrinos running down

00:35:19.560 --> 00:35:21.090
the green curve.

00:35:21.090 --> 00:35:24.720
They become mu neutrinos.

00:35:24.720 --> 00:35:28.740
And they change thereby
into mu neutrinos.

00:35:28.740 --> 00:35:32.130
And that means they
become unobservable

00:35:32.130 --> 00:35:40.365
because mu neutrinos can
only be changed into--

00:35:40.365 --> 00:35:43.290
in matter, they
could only be changed

00:35:43.290 --> 00:35:48.630
into mu mesons, which
have a mass of 100

00:35:48.630 --> 00:35:50.660
million electron watts.

00:35:50.660 --> 00:35:55.320
And no neutrino, which
is produced in the sun,

00:35:55.320 --> 00:35:57.510
has anything like that energy.

00:36:00.510 --> 00:36:06.840
So those neutrinos,
therefore, which

00:36:06.840 --> 00:36:16.310
are created at a density
above the crossing point,

00:36:16.310 --> 00:36:23.810
go down the green curve and end
up as unobservable mu neutrinos

00:36:23.810 --> 00:36:28.670
once they leave the
sun and come to Earth.

00:36:28.670 --> 00:36:34.010
And that would
explain how it comes

00:36:34.010 --> 00:36:42.566
that the neutrinos from the sun
are not observable on Earth.

00:36:45.380 --> 00:36:49.940
That clearly is going too far,
because after all, Mr. Davis

00:36:49.940 --> 00:36:55.910
did observe some neutrinos--
not enough, but some.

00:36:55.910 --> 00:36:57.560
And this is an important point.

00:37:01.480 --> 00:37:14.930
So conversely, if the
neutrino is made--

00:37:14.930 --> 00:37:19.100
has a lesser energy
than the density

00:37:19.100 --> 00:37:23.520
at the center of the sun,
it would be somewhere

00:37:23.520 --> 00:37:25.340
on this curve.

00:37:25.340 --> 00:37:32.180
Remember, what matters is
the product of the density

00:37:32.180 --> 00:37:34.100
times the electron--

00:37:34.100 --> 00:37:36.620
times the energy
of the neutrino.

00:37:36.620 --> 00:37:43.130
So neutrinos of lesser energy
than might be produced here.

00:37:43.130 --> 00:37:46.310
And [? SU ?] would
use the density

00:37:46.310 --> 00:37:49.670
as the neutrino
goes out of the sun.

00:37:49.670 --> 00:37:53.380
It goes down the periphery
curve and ends up

00:37:53.380 --> 00:37:56.930
as an electron neutrino.

00:37:56.930 --> 00:38:03.260
So the simplest conclusion,
which you may draw,

00:38:03.260 --> 00:38:14.920
is the high energy neutrinos
will be created here

00:38:14.920 --> 00:38:17.180
and will be unobservable.

00:38:17.180 --> 00:38:21.980
The lower energy neutrinos
will be created here,

00:38:21.980 --> 00:38:25.910
and will remain
electron neutrinos,

00:38:25.910 --> 00:38:31.700
and remain,
therefore, observable.

00:38:31.700 --> 00:38:36.740
That is the theory
of [? Michraiv ?]

00:38:36.740 --> 00:38:48.510
and [? Smirnov. ?] Some are
translated into different

00:38:48.510 --> 00:38:53.940
languages, quite apart from
being translated from Russian

00:38:53.940 --> 00:38:57.080
into English.

00:38:57.080 --> 00:38:59.795
And so, let's see
what we can conclude.

00:39:03.320 --> 00:39:13.110
For that, I go to the paper
which I mentioned before,

00:39:13.110 --> 00:39:18.710
which says that from
Boron 8, you get 4 SNU.

00:39:18.710 --> 00:39:24.590
From all other nuclei,
you get 1 and 1/2.

00:39:24.590 --> 00:39:28.460
Davis has observed 2.1.

00:39:28.460 --> 00:39:38.030
And so, I say, these neutrinos
are low energy neutrinos,

00:39:38.030 --> 00:39:40.330
and therefore are green--

00:39:40.330 --> 00:39:46.180
no, are purple-- and are
therefore observable.

00:39:46.180 --> 00:39:51.200
And also, a few of
the Boron 8 neutrinos

00:39:51.200 --> 00:39:56.960
must be observable, maybe 0.5,
plus or minus 0.5, not clear,

00:39:56.960 --> 00:40:02.540
whether any of them
need to be observable.

00:40:02.540 --> 00:40:07.330
I evaluated this wrongly.

00:40:07.330 --> 00:40:11.360
Fowler then corrected
me in a letter.

00:40:11.360 --> 00:40:16.360
And the result is
that the Boron 8

00:40:16.360 --> 00:40:23.030
neutrinos are observable if
they have less than 8MAB.

00:40:23.030 --> 00:40:31.100
And that leads to a difference
in mass square between the two

00:40:31.100 --> 00:40:37.560
types of neutrinos of 10 to the
minus 4 electron watts square.

00:40:37.560 --> 00:40:41.300
It means, by the way,
very importantly,

00:40:41.300 --> 00:40:47.240
this works only if the mu
neutrino has a higher mass

00:40:47.240 --> 00:40:50.450
than the electron neutrino.

00:40:50.450 --> 00:40:55.070
And so, if we assume tentatively
the electron neutrino

00:40:55.070 --> 00:40:58.290
has no mass, then
the mu neutrino

00:40:58.290 --> 00:41:05.470
would have a mass of one
hundredth of an electron watt,

00:41:05.470 --> 00:41:07.790
totally unobservable
by other means.

00:41:11.760 --> 00:41:16.800
Now, that's not
the only condition.

00:41:16.800 --> 00:41:19.362
You also need to have--

00:41:19.362 --> 00:41:23.520
as the neutrinos
go out of the sun,

00:41:23.520 --> 00:41:27.499
you have to have an
adiabatic transition.

00:41:27.499 --> 00:41:32.490
Well, that gives a
certain condition.

00:41:32.490 --> 00:41:38.040
And I will not bother
you with the details.

00:41:38.040 --> 00:41:40.510
It tells you that
the coupling angle--

00:41:44.840 --> 00:41:47.890
you'll remember,
electron neutrinos

00:41:47.890 --> 00:41:53.630
are cosine theta times Neu-1
plus sine theta, times Neu-2.

00:41:53.630 --> 00:42:00.660
But this coupling angle must be
greater than 0.01 radian, which

00:42:00.660 --> 00:42:03.960
is 0.6 degrees.

00:42:03.960 --> 00:42:08.250
It's almost certain if there
is a coupling angle at all

00:42:08.250 --> 00:42:11.100
that it will be greater
than this number.

00:42:11.100 --> 00:42:15.930
For instance, those of you who
would know particle physics

00:42:15.930 --> 00:42:21.390
will remember that the Cabibbo
angle is about 13 degrees,

00:42:21.390 --> 00:42:25.830
much, much larger
than 0.6 degrees.

00:42:25.830 --> 00:42:32.700
So it is essentially certain
that the angle is big enough.

00:42:32.700 --> 00:42:38.970
However, it says one very
important thing, namely

00:42:38.970 --> 00:42:45.480
that both neutrinos
must have mass.

00:42:45.480 --> 00:42:48.360
And that is not at all obvious.

00:42:48.360 --> 00:42:54.950
When we started talking about
neutrinos back 50 years ago,

00:42:54.950 --> 00:42:59.560
we thought, I think,
practically all of us,

00:42:59.560 --> 00:43:03.720
of neutrinos without any mass.

00:43:03.720 --> 00:43:09.990
And they have great
attraction, aesthetically.

00:43:09.990 --> 00:43:16.110
But I have no
preconceived notions,

00:43:16.110 --> 00:43:18.300
so I am perfectly satisfied.

00:43:18.300 --> 00:43:21.990
If neutrinos have some mass,
it will be very, very small.

00:43:28.250 --> 00:43:37.150
So if all this
theory is correct,

00:43:37.150 --> 00:43:40.400
then it says that we don't
observe those Boron 8

00:43:40.400 --> 00:43:43.200
neutrinos.

00:43:43.200 --> 00:43:50.910
And only the Boron
8 neutrinos are

00:43:50.910 --> 00:43:52.830
converted into mu neutrinos.

00:43:54.580 --> 00:44:00.250
And if you remember the table
I showed you at one time,

00:44:00.250 --> 00:44:05.410
if you use a gallium detector,
then you do not preferentially

00:44:05.410 --> 00:44:10.140
observe Boron 8 neutrinos,
but instead, you

00:44:10.140 --> 00:44:15.430
observe all neutrinos,
and particularly

00:44:15.430 --> 00:44:20.990
those coming directly from
the proton-proton reaction.

00:44:20.990 --> 00:44:25.040
So with a gallium
detector, you should

00:44:25.040 --> 00:44:29.770
observe essentially the same
as the theorists have always

00:44:29.770 --> 00:44:30.940
predicted.

00:44:30.940 --> 00:44:35.830
You should get the theoretical
result, which is about 110 SNU.

00:44:38.500 --> 00:44:43.870
So we have to hope
for the Europeans

00:44:43.870 --> 00:44:50.940
to get experiments with
the gallium detector.

00:44:50.940 --> 00:44:59.170
Well, I have shown you
the qualitative analytic

00:44:59.170 --> 00:45:02.440
discussion, which I have made.

00:45:02.440 --> 00:45:07.000
But there are people who are
much more industrious than I,

00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:11.080
and know how to use a
computer, which I don't.

00:45:11.080 --> 00:45:16.300
And they found, then, not only
one solution of the problem,

00:45:16.300 --> 00:45:18.720
but two.

00:45:18.720 --> 00:45:21.550
And the first
people who did that

00:45:21.550 --> 00:45:24.360
were the Russians themselves.

00:45:24.360 --> 00:45:28.180
And then with somewhat
improved technique,

00:45:28.180 --> 00:45:33.340
it was done by Rosen
and Gelb at Los Alamos,

00:45:33.340 --> 00:45:35.970
and got these results.

00:45:35.970 --> 00:45:39.790
Now, if you believe
that Davis observes

00:45:39.790 --> 00:45:43.670
one third of the
expected neutrinos,

00:45:43.670 --> 00:45:45.130
you should use the diamonds.

00:45:47.860 --> 00:45:52.540
The more recent ideas
of Bahcall are that he

00:45:52.540 --> 00:45:54.192
observed only a quarter.

00:45:54.192 --> 00:45:58.440
And then, you should
look at the [? circus. ?]

00:45:58.440 --> 00:46:03.850
And so what is plotted
here is delta m square

00:46:03.850 --> 00:46:10.180
in electron watts square, and 10
to the minus 4 is my solution.

00:46:10.180 --> 00:46:17.680
Constant mass, arbitrary
coupling angle, theta.

00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:20.380
But there is a second
solution, which

00:46:20.380 --> 00:46:25.240
is shown here with much
smaller mass difference.

00:46:25.240 --> 00:46:28.670
You would have thought 10 to
the minus 4 is small enough,

00:46:28.670 --> 00:46:39.070
but they get even less, but
with a definite relation

00:46:39.070 --> 00:46:45.370
between the mass difference
and the coupling angle.

00:46:45.370 --> 00:46:51.640
And in fact, the relation is
that the product of these two

00:46:51.640 --> 00:46:54.556
is a certain number.

00:46:54.556 --> 00:47:02.620
It is delta m squared times sine
square of the coupling angle,

00:47:02.620 --> 00:47:06.570
is 4 times 10 to the
minus 8 electron watts

00:47:06.570 --> 00:47:07.990
square, small enough.

00:47:13.130 --> 00:47:17.150
They have confirmed
the solution which I've

00:47:17.150 --> 00:47:19.435
published in addition to this.

00:47:22.230 --> 00:47:29.870
Now, if delta m squared is
less than my 10 to the minus 4,

00:47:29.870 --> 00:47:34.290
then also, neutrinos other
than the Boron neutrinos will

00:47:34.290 --> 00:47:36.580
be converted into mu neutrinos.

00:47:41.600 --> 00:47:47.870
But we know that we must have
some neutrinos left over,

00:47:47.870 --> 00:47:53.000
because after all, Davis
did observe one third or one

00:47:53.000 --> 00:47:55.850
quarter of the expected number.

00:47:55.850 --> 00:47:59.030
So there must be
some other condition

00:47:59.030 --> 00:48:06.770
which prevents the conversion
of the electron neutrinos

00:48:06.770 --> 00:48:08.240
into mu neutrinos.

00:48:08.240 --> 00:48:15.060
And that's the condition that
the transition be adiabatic.

00:48:15.060 --> 00:48:21.680
This was pointed out
not by Rosen and Gelb,

00:48:21.680 --> 00:48:26.710
but by Haxton of the
University of Washington.

00:48:26.710 --> 00:48:31.430
And he has shown that the
Rosen-Gelb solution essentially

00:48:31.430 --> 00:48:36.460
corresponds to the
adiabatic condition, which

00:48:36.460 --> 00:48:38.390
I mentioned before.

00:48:38.390 --> 00:48:45.650
And assuming that Haxton
finds analytically

00:48:45.650 --> 00:48:49.700
that this product should
be 6, 10 to the minus 8,

00:48:49.700 --> 00:48:53.540
close enough to the
4 10 to the minus 8

00:48:53.540 --> 00:48:57.180
that Rosen and Gelb had found.

00:49:00.970 --> 00:49:07.490
Now, because the low energy
neutrinos are now lost,

00:49:07.490 --> 00:49:11.050
the gallium experiment, which
measures mostly low energy

00:49:11.050 --> 00:49:15.400
neutrinos, will now
also give a response

00:49:15.400 --> 00:49:23.361
less than the original theory,
if the second solution is

00:49:23.361 --> 00:49:23.861
correct.

00:49:26.690 --> 00:49:34.510
I'll show you here a rather
nice curve of Rosen and Gelb,

00:49:34.510 --> 00:49:41.590
which tells you the
probability of reaching Earth

00:49:41.590 --> 00:49:46.840
as a function of
the energy in MAB.

00:49:46.840 --> 00:49:54.040
And there is the stars,
which is my solution.

00:49:54.040 --> 00:49:58.660
You have practically no
probability for the high energy

00:49:58.660 --> 00:50:01.520
neutrino, but all the
low energy neutrinos

00:50:01.520 --> 00:50:06.340
will remain electron
neutrinos and be observable.

00:50:06.340 --> 00:50:11.005
And contrary-wise, from
the Rosen-Gelb solution,

00:50:11.005 --> 00:50:12.830
it's the other way around.

00:50:15.800 --> 00:50:23.210
So the gallium
experiment therefore

00:50:23.210 --> 00:50:26.510
has become even more important.

00:50:26.510 --> 00:50:32.526
It will make it possible to
distinguish the two solutions.

00:50:36.494 --> 00:50:39.600
A question was raised,
is there any upper limit

00:50:39.600 --> 00:50:43.375
to sine square theta?

00:50:43.375 --> 00:50:46.950
This was investigated
by Suckley group,

00:50:46.950 --> 00:50:49.050
who found, yes, there is.

00:50:49.050 --> 00:50:53.800
The upper limit is
something like a half--

00:50:53.800 --> 00:50:57.000
well, two thirds, actually--

00:50:57.000 --> 00:51:00.392
essentially independent
of the mass. difference.

00:51:06.050 --> 00:51:14.810
The best calculation so far
has been made by two people

00:51:14.810 --> 00:51:22.540
at [? Feremy ?] Lab,
Park and Walker, who plot

00:51:22.540 --> 00:51:25.040
here some beautiful curves.

00:51:28.240 --> 00:51:35.305
It all uses the same
general idea, namely

00:51:35.305 --> 00:51:39.040
conversion of neutrinos
from electron neutrinos

00:51:39.040 --> 00:51:45.330
to mu neutrinos in the
sun due to high density

00:51:45.330 --> 00:51:46.750
of the matter in the sun.

00:51:49.370 --> 00:51:51.750
Plotted here is,
again, the difference

00:51:51.750 --> 00:51:55.630
in mass between the
two types of neutrinos.

00:51:55.630 --> 00:52:02.190
Plotted here is essentially
the sine square of 2 theta.

00:52:02.190 --> 00:52:08.190
And the contour lines correspond
to various possible results

00:52:08.190 --> 00:52:10.720
of the Davis experiment.

00:52:10.720 --> 00:52:14.620
What he gives is 2.1 SNU.

00:52:14.620 --> 00:52:17.480
That's this curve.

00:52:17.480 --> 00:52:19.950
But he says plus or minus 0.3.

00:52:19.950 --> 00:52:22.630
That's three times
more than error.

00:52:22.630 --> 00:52:27.920
So it can be anything
between 1.8 and 2.4.

00:52:27.920 --> 00:52:29.130
All right.

00:52:29.130 --> 00:52:32.420
If you follow the
2.1 curve, there's

00:52:32.420 --> 00:52:34.840
first a horizontal
[? sledge, ?] which

00:52:34.840 --> 00:52:39.930
is my attempt at a
minus 4 mass difference.

00:52:39.930 --> 00:52:44.380
Then there is the slant
line, which is essentially

00:52:44.380 --> 00:52:46.350
the Rosen-Gelb solution.

00:52:46.350 --> 00:52:53.465
It has a wiggle because
different types of neutrinos

00:52:53.465 --> 00:53:01.950
undergo the non-adiabatic
transition, which

00:53:01.950 --> 00:53:06.930
goes to smaller mass difference
and higher sine square theta.

00:53:06.930 --> 00:53:11.100
And finally, there
is the vertical line,

00:53:11.100 --> 00:53:20.610
which is essentially the Suckley
limit at high coupling angle.

00:53:20.610 --> 00:53:25.320
So this tells you, then, you
have essentially two solutions

00:53:25.320 --> 00:53:26.930
to the problem.

00:53:26.930 --> 00:53:30.990
Either the mass difference
is 10 to the minus 4,

00:53:30.990 --> 00:53:35.330
and then the coupling angle
can be anything, or else,

00:53:35.330 --> 00:53:39.000
the mass difference is much
less than 10 to the minus 4,

00:53:39.000 --> 00:53:43.530
and then the coupling angle
must be directly related

00:53:43.530 --> 00:53:50.300
to the mass difference.

00:53:50.300 --> 00:53:58.760
Well, the [? Feremy ?] Lab
people, Park and Walker,

00:53:58.760 --> 00:54:02.690
they went on and
discussed what should

00:54:02.690 --> 00:54:07.880
be the result of the gallium
experiment, once it is done.

00:54:07.880 --> 00:54:13.990
And that now is
particularly interesting.

00:54:13.990 --> 00:54:19.030
This, again, is mass
difference, angle,

00:54:19.030 --> 00:54:23.920
and the dotted lines are
the two limits of the Davis

00:54:23.920 --> 00:54:26.920
experiment with chlorine.

00:54:26.920 --> 00:54:33.820
The solid lines are the
contour lines for the gallium

00:54:33.820 --> 00:54:36.810
experiment to be done.

00:54:36.810 --> 00:54:40.600
And so, you see, if
the solution is along

00:54:40.600 --> 00:54:44.830
this line, or along
this line, then

00:54:44.830 --> 00:54:48.670
the gallium experiment
should give, oh,

00:54:48.670 --> 00:54:53.660
somewhere between 100-120 SNU.

00:54:53.660 --> 00:55:00.550
But if the solution is the type
preferred by Rosen and Gelb,

00:55:00.550 --> 00:55:08.350
then the gallium experiment
will give you a greatly reduced

00:55:08.350 --> 00:55:15.700
count, maybe as low as 10 SNU,
10 percent of the theoretically

00:55:15.700 --> 00:55:19.020
predicted number.

00:55:19.020 --> 00:55:22.210
So this is extremely
interesting, and makes,

00:55:22.210 --> 00:55:24.520
of course, the
gallium experiment

00:55:24.520 --> 00:55:28.366
more and more important.

00:55:28.366 --> 00:55:39.040
And so what can we conclude?

00:55:39.040 --> 00:55:42.400
If the gallium experiment
gives the high value,

00:55:42.400 --> 00:55:49.310
about 100 SNU, then there
are two alternatives.

00:55:49.310 --> 00:55:53.780
Either my original
interpretation of the two--

00:55:53.780 --> 00:55:59.000
of the Russian suggestion
is the right one,

00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:02.270
the mass difference
is 10 to the minus 4

00:56:02.270 --> 00:56:08.300
and the angle is
undetermined, or there

00:56:08.300 --> 00:56:14.240
is some totally unknown
other explanation.

00:56:14.240 --> 00:56:18.770
Now, Bahcall swears
that his theory

00:56:18.770 --> 00:56:23.750
of the temperature distribution
of the sun is correct.

00:56:26.650 --> 00:56:31.570
So it's very unlikely that
there is another explanation.

00:56:31.570 --> 00:56:36.970
However, one would have to
say, if gallium gives 100 SNU

00:56:36.970 --> 00:56:43.510
or so, then the
[? Michraiv-Smirnov ?]

00:56:43.510 --> 00:56:47.350
explanation is merely likely.

00:56:47.350 --> 00:56:51.040
It is not absolutely proved.

00:56:51.040 --> 00:57:00.780
But if the gallium experiment
gives a much lower number--

00:57:00.780 --> 00:57:09.790
let us say, something less than
60, perhaps as low as 10 SNU--

00:57:09.790 --> 00:57:20.560
then that can only be explained
by the Russian suggestion,

00:57:20.560 --> 00:57:25.390
because there is nothing that
we can do about the distribution

00:57:25.390 --> 00:57:31.450
of temperature in the sun,
which would reduce the number

00:57:31.450 --> 00:57:33.280
of quote, unquote,
[? "unreactions," ?]

00:57:33.280 --> 00:57:39.620
because those reactions
give us our light.

00:57:39.620 --> 00:57:43.570
We know exactly how much
energy the sun emits.

00:57:43.570 --> 00:57:49.060
And so, we know exactly how
many proton-proton correlations

00:57:49.060 --> 00:57:50.250
occur.

00:57:50.250 --> 00:57:58.520
And therefore, no change of the
solar temperature distribution

00:57:58.520 --> 00:58:03.580
could explain the gallium
result anywhere in that region.

00:58:03.580 --> 00:58:15.220
In that case, then, the
Michraiv-Smirnov answer theory

00:58:15.220 --> 00:58:18.370
is definitely proved.

00:58:18.370 --> 00:58:26.240
And we must then assume
that, indeed, neutrinos

00:58:26.240 --> 00:58:29.810
have a mass, that the
mass of the mu neutrino

00:58:29.810 --> 00:58:34.010
is greater than that of
the electron neutrino.

00:58:34.010 --> 00:58:40.010
And how much it is can
be determined, then,

00:58:40.010 --> 00:58:42.877
from the gallium experiment.

00:58:47.170 --> 00:58:53.950
If the gallium experiment
gives the high value,

00:58:53.950 --> 00:58:58.930
then one probably
has to do still

00:58:58.930 --> 00:59:08.050
another experiment showing
that it is, indeed,

00:59:08.050 --> 00:59:14.410
the Russian suggestion
and not something

00:59:14.410 --> 00:59:20.620
funny about the sun
that gives the--

00:59:20.620 --> 00:59:28.220
that is the cause
of the Davis result.

00:59:28.220 --> 00:59:32.210
If gallium is as
low as about 10 SNU,

00:59:32.210 --> 00:59:36.670
then delta m square is of
order 10 to the minus 6,

00:59:36.670 --> 00:59:41.000
and sine square of 2-theta
is of the order of 0.1.

00:59:41.000 --> 00:59:43.470
And that's very
close to the Cabibbo

00:59:43.470 --> 00:59:46.990
angle, which would be 0.16.

00:59:46.990 --> 00:59:50.280
There is no good reason why
it should be just the Cabibbo

00:59:50.280 --> 00:59:50.780
angle.

00:59:53.330 --> 00:59:59.630
Now, the most exciting part of
this whole story [INAUDIBLE]

00:59:59.630 --> 01:00:06.050
is that it might permit
us a glimpse into the gut.

01:00:06.050 --> 01:00:10.590
And by this, I don't
mean the intestines.

01:00:10.590 --> 01:00:14.720
But I mean the
grand unified theory

01:00:14.720 --> 01:00:17.870
that particle
theorists are fond of,

01:00:17.870 --> 01:00:21.174
and of which I
understand nothing.

01:00:21.174 --> 01:00:23.660
[LAUGHTER]

01:00:23.660 --> 01:00:28.670
However, all particle
theorists tell me

01:00:28.670 --> 01:00:36.010
that in gut, there
should be right handed

01:00:36.010 --> 01:00:39.500
neutrinos in addition
to the ones we know,

01:00:39.500 --> 01:00:42.530
which are left handed neutrinos.

01:00:42.530 --> 01:00:44.720
And these right handed
neutrinos should

01:00:44.720 --> 01:00:50.240
have a mass about equal
to the grand unification

01:00:50.240 --> 01:00:58.890
mass, which is 10 to the
14 GEV, or 10 to the 23 EV.

01:00:58.890 --> 01:01:01.420
So we are talking
at the same time

01:01:01.420 --> 01:01:06.350
about terribly small masses
and terribly big masses.

01:01:06.350 --> 01:01:13.730
There is a particular theory
by Gell-Mann and two others,

01:01:13.730 --> 01:01:17.760
simultaneously
obtained by Yanagida,

01:01:17.760 --> 01:01:25.840
'78 and '79, according to
which, the mass of neutrinos

01:01:25.840 --> 01:01:31.710
of a given [? flavor ?] [? I ?]
should be the mass squared

01:01:31.710 --> 01:01:38.580
of the corresponding quark
divided by some constant

01:01:38.580 --> 01:01:44.940
and the mass of the
grand unification theory.

01:01:44.940 --> 01:01:47.710
Of course, that
mass nobody knows.

01:01:47.710 --> 01:01:52.170
But it is about that number.

01:01:52.170 --> 01:01:56.298
Why the K appears there,
I haven't any idea.

01:01:56.298 --> 01:02:00.280
[LAUGHTER]

01:02:00.280 --> 01:02:02.200
The Michraivs
neutrino would have 10

01:02:02.200 --> 01:02:08.390
to the minus 6 EV, and the tau
neutrino 10 to the minus 3 EV,

01:02:08.390 --> 01:02:10.680
with the right handed
neutrinos having

01:02:10.680 --> 01:02:15.460
a mass like the gut mass.

01:02:15.460 --> 01:02:20.650
It is obvious that the mu
neutrino would then not

01:02:20.650 --> 01:02:28.560
be enough to satisfy any
solution of the solar neutrino

01:02:28.560 --> 01:02:30.590
puzzle.

01:02:30.590 --> 01:02:33.910
Only the tau neutrino would.

01:02:33.910 --> 01:02:39.200
The difference of the square of
the tau neutrino and E neutrino

01:02:39.200 --> 01:02:42.040
mass would be 10
to the minus 6 EV

01:02:42.040 --> 01:02:47.530
square, which falls
right into the range

01:02:47.530 --> 01:02:52.390
of the Rosen-Gelb solution.

01:02:52.390 --> 01:02:55.630
And it falls right
at the place where

01:02:55.630 --> 01:03:03.580
gallium would give the minimum
response of about 10 SNU.

01:03:03.580 --> 01:03:11.340
So we must then assume
that, in the sun,

01:03:11.340 --> 01:03:16.110
the electron neutrino converts
into a tau neutrino, not

01:03:16.110 --> 01:03:18.300
a mu neutrino.

01:03:18.300 --> 01:03:20.880
At present, I don't
know any experiment

01:03:20.880 --> 01:03:24.540
which would distinguish
between tau and mu neutrino

01:03:24.540 --> 01:03:27.270
as the product.

01:03:27.270 --> 01:03:31.410
But you can see
that it will be most

01:03:31.410 --> 01:03:37.560
exciting to have the result
of the gallium experiment.

01:03:37.560 --> 01:03:43.960
This can, first of all,
show whether or not

01:03:43.960 --> 01:03:50.210
the [? Michraiv-Smirnov ?]
suggestion is correct,

01:03:50.210 --> 01:03:57.150
and whether this is the solution
of the solar neutrino puzzle.

01:03:57.150 --> 01:04:01.650
And secondly, it may
give us an insight

01:04:01.650 --> 01:04:05.010
into grand unified
theory, and insight

01:04:05.010 --> 01:04:13.020
into things which occur at
energies of 10 to the 14 GEV,

01:04:13.020 --> 01:04:19.140
energies which surely are
beyond the most ambitious plans

01:04:19.140 --> 01:04:23.630
of accelerators, and surely--

01:04:23.630 --> 01:04:28.830
and which also are beyond the
range of cosmic ray neutrinos.

01:04:28.830 --> 01:04:34.740
They go up to about 10 to the 20
EV, whereas the gut is about 10

01:04:34.740 --> 01:04:37.320
to the 23 EV.

01:04:37.320 --> 01:04:42.900
So there is a good
chance, I believe,

01:04:42.900 --> 01:04:52.980
that the neutrinos will give
us a look into energies so high

01:04:52.980 --> 01:04:59.220
that we have no reasonable
expectation of reaching them

01:04:59.220 --> 01:05:02.610
by accelerators or
other observations.

01:05:02.610 --> 01:05:08.880
And if that is so, then
it was most fortunate

01:05:08.880 --> 01:05:15.210
that Ray Davis did not
observe the neutrinos that

01:05:15.210 --> 01:05:21.180
were expected, but observed
only a small fraction of them.

01:05:21.180 --> 01:05:25.620
And no matter how much
the theorists pressed him,

01:05:25.620 --> 01:05:29.280
he still stuck to
his small number.

01:05:29.280 --> 01:05:34.560
And this may have shown us
a very interesting feature

01:05:34.560 --> 01:05:42.090
of neutrino physics, and
possibly, the best [? hand ?]

01:05:42.090 --> 01:05:47.370
at knowing something about the
very highest energy particle

01:05:47.370 --> 01:05:48.330
physics.

01:05:48.330 --> 01:05:49.230
Thank you.

01:05:49.230 --> 01:05:51.080
[APPLAUSE]

